{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-progress bias, routes every obstacle event through a dedicated recovery state, uses backward motion only as a one-shot response to front obstacles, prefers directed turns away from side obstacles, and reserves full_rotate for repeated blocked-front situations as a last resort. Action states self-loop on path_clear so intended open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate environment sensing from motion capability in G so E can impose a safe exploration policy cleanly.",
    "Use perception states for uncontrollable branching and one-shot action states with exactly one controllable event to respect DES control structure and open-loop pulse semantics."
  ],
